today we're talking about new dead space  remake details war zone on mobile and  more  the dead space remake from ea motive is  now targeting an early 2023 release  while this doesn't constitute a delay  since the game was never given a public  release window it had been previously  reportedly targeting a 2022 release just  ahead of the dead space live stream  where the release window was announced  reports had circulated of the impending  kind of delay ea is said to be impressed  with the remake but wants it to be as  well received as capcom's resident evil  remakes as for the stream it featured an  in-depth look at some of the audio  systems used to create the creepy  atmosphere and things like the alive  system which has isaac struggling to  breathe the team will be hosting another  stream in may focusing on the art design  originally developed by visceral games  back in 2008 dead space is a fan  favorite and helped reinvigorate the  horror genre in games the remake is  being handled by ea motive the studio  behind star wars squadrons and it will  run on the frostbite engine and don't  worry i have the perfect thing to hold  you over until that game releases the  new dino safari dlc for lawn mowing sim  i don't know about you but that looks  like a roaring good time to me  however maybe you'd rather lay in bed  and throw stones at people in the gulag  while a new blog post on the official  call of duty website has confirmed that  call of duty warzone is coming to mobile  unfortunately though the post is light  on information this confirmation comes  after a report from december 2021 hinted  at a 2022 release date for the warzone's  mobile version tom henderson tweeted  that the game was anticipated for launch  this year citing its addition to the  playtest cloud database warzone will  mark the second call of duty battle  royale on mobile devices joining the  mode built into the standalone call of  duty mobile there's no word yet on  whether or not this new mobile war zone  will be a part of that app or launch as  a separate download and while we're on  the subject of handheld games let's talk  about steam deck microsoft has detailed  which of its games are compatible with  valve steam deck with only a handful of  titles being unsupported due to  incompatibility with anti-cheat software  in a post on steam microsoft explained  that each developer in xbox game studios  is responsible for ensuring  compatibility with the steam deck but  that priorities at each might force this  to take longer than expected the upside  is that many games are already  compatible with a large majority having  verified statuses already from valve in  terms of games that will not work at all  on the steam deck halo infinite and the  master chief collection are both  unsupported as well as gears of war 5  and microsoft flight simulator 10.  unlike bungie which says players  attempting to play destiny 2 on steam  deck might result in a ban microsoft  hasn't detailed what exactly might  happen if you try to get games like halo  working on steam os so proceed with  caution alright the weekend's here so  let me know what you're playing and head  over to twitter and tweet me some  screenshots i'd love to see your  gametography like this moment from our  very own aaron sampson  see you next week
 

